kill - send a signal

SYNOPSIS
    kill [-SIGNAL] PID...
           kill -l

DESCRIPTION
    The signal defaults to TERM. It may be a number or a name, with or
    without the SIG.

    A negative pid is a process group - `kill -TERM -42` ends every process
    of job 42. That is the form that matters, because a pipeline is several
    processes and ending one of them is not ending it.

      -l   list the signals

SEE ALSO
    ps, jobs, sh
